{
  "an8.48:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.48 ",
  "an8.48:0.2": "5. Sabbath ",
  "an8.48:0.3": "With Nakula’s Mother on the Agreeable Gods ",
  "an8.48:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Bhaggas at Crocodile’s Bellow, in the deer park at Bhesakaḷā’s Wood. ",
  "an8.48:1.2": "Then the housewife Nakula’s mother went up to the Buddha, bowed, and sat down to one side. The Buddha said to her: ",
  "an8.48:2.1": "“Nakula’s mother, when they have eight qualities ladies—when their body breaks up, after death—are reborn in company with the Gods of the Agreeable Host. ",
  "an8.48:2.2": "What eight? ",
  "an8.48:2.3": "Take the case of a lady whose mother and father give her to a husband wanting what’s best for her, out of kindness and sympathy. She would get up before him and go to bed after him, and be obliging, behaving nicely and speaking politely. ",
  "an8.48:3.1": "She honors, respects, esteems, and venerates those her husband respects, such as ",
  "an8.48:3.2": "mother and father, and ascetics and brahmins. ",
  "an8.48:3.3": "And when they arrive she serves them with a seat and water. ",
  "an8.48:4.1": "She’s deft and tireless in her husband’s household duties, such as knitting and sewing. She understands how to go about things in order to complete and organize the work. ",
  "an8.48:5.1": "She knows what work her husband’s domestic bondservants, servants, and workers have completed, and what they’ve left incomplete. ",
  "an8.48:5.2": "She knows who is sic